<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="rings">Rings</h3>There is a clear winner combination of rings in this phase (not only for fashion sake), namely <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45495/conductive-seal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_66.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conductive Seal</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46046/nebula-band">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_70.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nebula Band</span></a>, although if you are in dire need of hit rating <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45297/shimmering-seal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_63.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shimmering Seal</span></a> also performs great.<br/>
<br/>It should be noted that the normal mode rings are only slightly better compared to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40399/signet-of-manifested-pain">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_51naxxramas.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of Manifested Pain</span></a>, the best ring of the previous phase.<br/>
<br/>Also of note is the newly upgraded <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45691/inscribed-signet-of-the-kirin-tor">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_73.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Signet of the Kirin Tor</span></a>, costing a further 1000g on top of the hefty 8000g cost of the tier 7 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44935/ring-of-the-kirin-tor">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_74.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of the Kirin Tor</span></a>. Benefitting from general Ulduar ilvl buffs, this ring outcompetes the Tier 7 best in slot option <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40719/band-of-channeled-magic">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_68.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of Channeled Magic</span></a> by a small margin, and may be a consideration for high rollers looking to squeeze out a bit more damage on progression.<div class="box">
<b>Ring Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44636/enchant-ring-greater-spellpower">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Ring - Greater Spellpower</span></a> (<a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=333/enchanting">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchanting</span></a>).</div>
