<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="1-handed-weapons">1-Handed Weapons</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45620/starshard-edge">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Starshard Edge</span></a> from 25-man Algalon leaves our Phase 1 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40396/the-turning-tide">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_130.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Turning Tide</span></a> in the dust. It was already a strong weapon back in the day, but with the big ilvl buff Ulduar loot has seen this time around, it will be all the more desirable.<br/>
<br/>The closest alternative is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45990/fusion-blade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_132.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fusion Blade</span></a> from 10-man Hard Mode <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=33350/mimiron">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Mimiron</span></a>, but the extra hit and lack of spirit on this item makes it less attractive for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warlock.gif");'></span>
<span class="c9">Affliction Warlocks</span>. Note that both of these have a good chunk of hit rating on them, something to keep in mind when swapping from <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40396/the-turning-tide">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_130.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Turning Tide</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45990/fusion-blade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_132.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fusion Blade</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45437/runescribed-blade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_134.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runescribed Blade</span></a> both deserve honorable mention as crit-swapping weapons. They have slightly more crit rating without sacrificing a significant amount of other stats (which also have value before you have applied <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=47813/corruption">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_abominationexplosion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corruption</span></a>). <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/warlock/affliction/dps-rotation-cooldowns-abilities-pve#weaponswap">To learn more about weapon swapping see the Affliction rotation guide.</a>
